    "description": "Neoen develops, owns, and operates renewable energy and storage assets, with activities spanning utility-scale solar, wind, and battery storage. Its revenue base is largely contracted through long-term power purchase agreements and regulated or contracted capacity arrangements, giving the platform an infrastructure-style operating profile. In North America the company has active operations and development in Canada and Mexico, including battery storage and solar projects, while its broader footprint extends across Europe, Australia, and Latin America. Neoen states that it was founded in 2008, and Brookfield’s 2025 offer materials described a portfolio with more than 8 GW in operation or under construction worldwide. Brookfield acquired control through a 2025 public offer, while Temasek disclosed that it partnered in the investment and held a minority interest in the acquisition structure.",
